{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "WRFCBMZDryDepAssignment",
    "description": "The CBM-Z gas dry-deposition velocities WRF-Chem actually uses: wesely_driver's per-slot velocities (ddvel0d, deposition_velocity.esm's vd) after the reassignments wesely_driver makes for the CBM-Z family of mechanisms (chem/module_dep_simple.F of WRF v4.8.0, lines 404-444 for every CBM-Z chem_opt and 524-536 for chem_opt = 170 CBMZ_MOSAIC_KPP). These are what dry_dep_driver hands vertmx as the lower-boundary deposition velocity of each gas.\n\nThe code's own comment says what the reassignments are: 'For the additional CBMZ species, assign similar RADM counter parts for now. Short lived species get a zero velocity since dry dep should be unimportant. ALSO, treat p_sulf as h2so4 vapor, not aerosol sulfate.' Concretely: sulf and hcl take hno3's velocity; ch3oh and c2h5oh take hcho's; open takes xyl's; op3 takes op2's; and the peroxy radicals (ch3o2, ethp, to2, cro, c2o3, ro2, ano2, nap, xo2, xpar), isoprd, isopp, isopn, isopo2 and the ten SOA-precursor gases of chem_opt 170 (aro1, aro2, alk1, ole1, api1, api2, lim1, lim2, api, lim) get zero. Every other gas keeps its own Wesely velocity.\n\nThat list is a table, `source_slot`: for each gas slot, the slot whose Wesely velocity it takes, with 0 for 'none'. It is data in exactly the sense the Fortran's assignment statements are, so it is written as one, and the one equation applies it.\n\nThe species axis is the 65 gas slots of chem_opt = 170 in WRF's p_* numbering (slot 1 is the unused dummy slot; its row is the identity so that the table has no hole), so a consumer that mounts deposition_velocity.esm over the same axis (igas = 1..65) can feed its vd straight in.\n\nTests: the in-model chem170 reference (dumps/chem170_wrf). Input: ddvel0d from the wesely hook (inside wesely_driver, before the reassignments); expected: the ddvel that the chem_vertmx hook records entering vertmx at the same step. The table reproduces all 65 gas velocities bit for bit at every one of the 16 dumped steps; three are asserted.",
    "authors": [
      "EqWeFiC"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "wrf-chem",
      "dry-deposition",
      "wesely",
      "cbm-z",
      "chem_opt-170"
    ]
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "NSPEC": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 65,
      "description": "Gas slots of chem_opt = 170, numgas = 65 (slot 1 is the dummy)."
    }
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "spc": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": "NSPEC"
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "WRFCBMZDryDepAssignment": {
      "variables": {
        "vd_wesely": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m/s",
          "shape": [
            "spc"
          ],
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Wesely's deposition velocity of every gas slot, ddvel0d (deposition_velocity.esm's vd with igas = the slot)."
        },
        "source_slot": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "spc"
          ],
          "description": "The gas slot whose Wesely velocity each slot takes, 0 for a gas WRF does not deposit. Slot (name): 1 (dummy) 1; 2 so2 2; 3 sulf 7 (= hno3); 4-34 (no2 ... ho2) themselves; 35 hcl 7 (= hno3); 36 ch3o2 0; 37 ethp 0; 38 ch3oh 10 (= hcho); 39 c2h5oh 10 (= hcho); 40 par 40; 41 to2 0; 42 cro 0; 43 open 25 (= xyl); 44 op3 12 (= op2); 45 c2o3 0; 46 ro2 0; 47 ano2 0; 48 nap 0; 49 xo2 0; 50 xpar 0; 51 isoprd 0; 52 isopp 0; 53 isopn 0; 54 ch4 54; 55-64 aro1, aro2, alk1, ole1, api1, api2, lim1, lim2, api, lim 0; 65 isopo2 0. (module_dep_simple.F:420-443, 524-536.)"
        },
        "vd": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m/s",
          "shape": [
            "spc"
          ],
          "description": "The deposition velocity of each gas slot that dry_dep_driver hands vertmx (ddvel(:,:,1:numgas))."
        }
      },
